{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce new legal protections for access to purchased video games",
        "additional_details": "The Government should strengthen UK consumer law so people who buy digital games retain fair long term access if a store closes, a licence changes, or content is removed.\r\n \r\nCompanies should be required to give clear notice before access changes and provide a permanent download, offline option, physical release, refund, or fair alternative where possible.\r\n",
        "background": "Introduce new legal protections requiring video games sold in the UK to remain accessible to consumers who have purchased them. This could involve a requirement to provide physical versions or equivalent permanent ownership options for software.",
